            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) Have you able to reproduce this on linux? My best guess on this is some wacky behaviour around pager on the OpenBSD implementation of `mandoc`\n\nYes, I did manage to reproduce this yesterday with `mandoc`. Although I was confused with \"Arch linux with `mandoc`, `man-pages` packages.\", since `pacman` doesn't allow me to install both of them at the same time.\n\nI could not find a reliable way to fix this, so decided to pivot to fully rely on `:Man` command to preview and choose. This lifts the burden from 'mini.extra' to adjust to all of these system+tool specific quirks.\n\nThere is a hope to push temporary branch for you to test: @itsthomashere - for your Arch case, @pkazmier - on MacOS (just in case).",
